---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/base-layout.astro';
import CoverageExplorer from '../components/coverage-explorer.astro';
import CommandPalette from '../components/command-palette.astro';
import { catalogueSummary } from '@attestor/findings/catalogue';

const summary = catalogueSummary();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What we test"
  description="The complete check catalogue Attestor Security runs from: every check, what it finds, how it is done, and the OWASP WSTG, ASVS, MASVS and LLM Top 10 identifier it maps to."
  path="/what-we-test"
  ogImage="/og/what-we-test.png"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <p class="eyebrow">Coverage</p>
      <h1>Every check we run, published</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is not a marketing summary of our capabilities. It is the actual catalogue the platform
        runs from, imported into this page at build time. If a check is removed from the platform it
        disappears from here on the next deploy.
      </p>

      <dl class="summary">
        <div>
          <dt>Checks</dt>
          <dd class="numeric">{summary.total}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Automated</dt>
          <dd class="numeric">{summary.byAutomation.automated ?? 0}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Tool-assisted, human-judged</dt>
          <dd class="numeric">{summary.byAutomation.assisted ?? 0}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Manual</dt>
          <dd class="numeric">{summary.byAutomation.manual ?? 0}</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <p class="note">
        The manual and tool-assisted counts are the important ones. Anything marked automated is
        something you could buy a subscription for; the rest is the work. Every automated finding
        still passes through a human before it can appear in a report.
      </p>

      <CoverageExplorer />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CommandPalette />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  .summary {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-m);
    margin: var(--space-l) 0 var(--space-s);
    padding-top: var(--space-m);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .summary dt {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .summary dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .note {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-s);
  }
</style>
